  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.doc",
    "value": "D is dense in a preorder I when every pair a < b brackets a point of D, that is, when there is d ∈ D with a ≤ d ≤ b. On a linear order without jumps this agrees with strict betweenness; on an order with jumps it is strictly weaker, and it is the form under which ded bounds the size of the order."
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.pretty",
    "value": "{I : Type u_1} → [Preorder I] → Set I → Prop"
