  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.kind",
    "value": "def"
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.doc",
    "value": "D is strictly dense in a preorder I when every pair a < b has a point of D strictly between them. This is the second of the two readings of \"dense subset\" that the definition of ded in the literature leaves open; the first is IsDenseIn. Where the order has no jumps the two agree, and a linear order with a jump whose two endpoints lie in D satisfies IsDenseIn only. The literature on ded does not say which reading is meant; ded'_eq_ded shows the question does not affect the value of ded at an infinite cardinal."
  },
  {
    "field": "dictionary_constant.pretty",
    "value": "{I : Type u_1} → [Preorder I] → Set I → Prop"
